    "options": {
      "A": "Answer \"base\", naming that word instead of using a base–height product.",
      "B": "Use $PQ=8$ cm with a slanted side from $R$ that is not perpendicular to the line through $PQ$.",
      "C": "Take base $PQ=8$ cm and perpendicular height $RH=5$ cm, so area $=\\frac{1}{2}\\times 8\\times 5=20$ cm$^{2}$.",
      "D": "Treat the question as finding a triangle's perimeter from the three side lengths, outside this area hinge."
